# Reference/input material — each is its own git repo or a raw firmware dump,
# not part of this project's history.
/android_kernel_samsung_gts9/
/ubuntu-galaxy-tab-s9ultra/
/sm-x800-linux/
/2026-09-04--*/

# vendor-firmware-dump/ and buildroot/firmware-overlay/ (below) used to be
# gitignored here as proprietary/not-ours-to-redistribute. Per explicit user
# decision (Networking bring-up session, 2026-09-07 -- see
# docs/porting-log.md), both are now committed anyway so the whole build is
# reproducible from this repo alone without a from-scratch device pull; the
# redistribution-rights caveat still applies to vendor-firmware-dump/'s
# contents (Samsung/Qualcomm's own binaries, not authored by this project)
# and is documented there and in docs/hardware-facts.md, not re-litigated
# here.
#
# Exception: several vendor-firmware-dump/firmware/<dir>/<dir>/ subpaths
# (qca6490, abov, keyboard_stm, mfc, tsp_stm -- confirmed byte-identical to
# their own parent directory's files via `cmp`) are duplicates caused by a
# real `adb pull` directory-nesting bug in an earlier version of
# scripts/extract-vendor-firmware.sh (fixed there; the already-doubled files
# on disk were kept per explicit user instruction, "no need to remove it
# just keep it") -- excluded here rather than committed twice for no reason.
/vendor-firmware-dump/firmware/qca6490/qca6490/
/vendor-firmware-dump/firmware/abov/abov/
/vendor-firmware-dump/firmware/keyboard_stm/keyboard_stm/
/vendor-firmware-dump/firmware/mfc/mfc/
/vendor-firmware-dump/firmware/tsp_stm/tsp_stm/

# buildroot/firmware-overlay/ (staged by scripts/fetch-ath11k-firmware.sh --
# a mix of upstream linux-firmware.git content and, for BT, files copied
# from this device's own vendor-firmware-dump/) is now committed too, see
# the note above.

# Build scratch and output
/work/
/out/

# Fetched mainline kernel source (pinned via scripts/fetch-mainline.sh, not vendored —
# too large to commit; docs/hardware-facts.md records the exact pinned commit instead)
/kernel/linux/

# Fetched uniLoader source (pinned via scripts/fetch-uniloader.sh, not vendored —
# active upstream project; our own board/SoC additions live in uniloader-overlay/
# instead, which IS committed)
/uniloader/upstream/

# Fetched Buildroot source (pinned via scripts/fetch-buildroot.sh, not vendored —
# active upstream project; our own board config/overlay live in buildroot/configs/
# and buildroot/rootfs-overlay/ instead, which ARE committed)
/buildroot/upstream/

# Large binary artifacts — never commit these, they're build output
*.img
*.win
*.win.md5
*.dtb
*.dtbo
Image.gz*
*.ko
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tar.xz

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code session state
/.claude/

# Real WiFi credentials for the bring-up rootfs (Networking bring-up
# session) — private, never committed; see
# buildroot/rootfs-overlay/etc/wpa_supplicant.conf's own header comment.
# The tracked file in git stays the PLACEHOLDER_SSID/PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD
# version; this ignore rule only takes effect once it's overwritten
# in-place with real credentials for a local build.
/buildroot/rootfs-overlay/etc/wpa_supplicant.conf

# Same treatment, for the Fedora rootfs's NetworkManager connection
# profiles (gts9wifi-fedora pivot, scripts/build-fedora-rootfs.sh) — real
# SSID/PSK/UUID, never committed. The tracked files stay the
# PLACEHOLDER_SSID/PLACEHOLDER_PASSWORD/.example versions. "home" (the
# original network) and "guest" (an open network at a different
# location, added Session 9) are both kept — see docs/porting-log.md.
/buildroot/rootfs-overlay/etc/NetworkManager-system-connection.nmconnection
/buildroot/rootfs-overlay/etc/NetworkManager-system-connection-guest.nmconnection
